        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-17T09:39:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One of the reasons I can think of is that Styles of Meditation which allow you to search for the style you desire in both the deck and trash. Where Tools can't be searched for at all. However you can retrieve all equipment cards with Salvage Yard, at the same time though since tools don't usually get destroyed it isn't too common to retrieve a lot of your equipment cards from the trash</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Your friends will love you for it and love you even more if you can keep the grease gun going since it's an equipment. But yeah I believe it's meditation's existence that is the defining factor and to diversify mechanics so tools and style dont play the same but complement each other. Fixer has his shining moments either way last game I played with him a player whined I was stealing all the sunshine with fixer I was laughing thinking on how people perceive fixer on this forum.</p>",
